  <data key="d4">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d5">The constant inner potential method uses the local electrode inner potential, rather than the global Fermi level, as the thermodynamic parameter for electrode potential.</data>
  <data key="d6">thermodynamic parameter assignment</data>
  <data key="d7">The constant inner potential method uses the local electrode inner potential, rather than the global Fermi level, as the thermodynamic parameter for electrode potential.</data>
  <data key="d8">computational</data>
  <data key="d9">This is the defining methodological distinction of CIP.</data>
  <data key="d10">["claim_cip_electrode_parameter"]</data>
