<node id="paper::broad_0774386e5705dc5099bf::claim_cip_general applicability">
  <data key="d4">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d5">The constant inner potential approach is more versatile than the constant Fermi-level GCE-DFT approach because it can be applied to outer-sphere reactions and biased two-electrode systems.</data>
  <data key="d6">methodological applicability</data>
  <data key="d7">The constant inner potential approach is more versatile than the constant Fermi-level GCE-DFT approach because it can be applied to outer-sphere reactions and biased two-electrode systems.</data>
  <data key="d8">computational</data>
  <data key="d9">The abstract states that numerical and analytical studies demonstrate this broader applicability.</data>
  <data key="d10">["claim_cip_general applicability"]</data>
  <data key="d11">1</data>
  <data key="d12">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
  <data key="d13">broad_abstract_support</data>
  <data key="d14">True</data>
  <data key="d15">abstract</data>
